@startuml runtime_control_polling
title Durable execution control polling
' Java baseline: 043fad7cc1e63b419b7099d22b1db14500a2182f.
' Polling implementation: fccf1c2f; source slice bfc90fc4.
' Java source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/ExecutionControlPollingService.java#poll.
' Java source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeLocalControlDispatcher.java.
' Java source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeExecutionControlRepository.java#findPendingControls.
' SQL source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/mapper/session/RuntimeExecutionControlMapper.xml#findPendingControls.
' pi baseline: 4af9d21d3b4d664e4a29fcabfec85171077248e3.
' pi source: packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts#runAgentLoop and #prepareToolCall.
' Observed behavior: Java and pi cancellation objects are local to one process.
' Design reason: query durable controls only for exact executions held by this instance.
' Java divergence: database polling is a CampusClaw cross-instance architecture change.
participant Scheduler
participant ExecutionControlPollingService as Poller
participant RuntimeLocalControlDispatcher as Dispatcher
participant RuntimeExecutionControlRepository as Repository
database "Control tables" as Database
participant "Dispatch executor" as Executor
participant "Exact local execution" as Runtime

Scheduler -> Poller : poll
Poller -> Dispatcher : activeTargets(maxActive)
alt no local targets
  Dispatcher --> Poller : empty
  note right of Poller
    No database query
  end note
else exact local targets
  Dispatcher --> Poller : distinct bounded targets
  loop per bounded batch
    Poller -> Repository : findPendingControls(targets)
    Repository -> Database : match execution, stop, confirmation
    Database --> Repository : committed signals only
    Repository --> Poller : control signals
    loop per signal
      alt stop is committed
        Poller -> Executor : dispatch stop
        Executor -> Dispatcher : dispatchStop(exact target)
      else pending confirmation
        Poller -> Executor : dispatch confirmation
        Executor -> Dispatcher : dispatchConfirmation(target, toolCallId)
      end
      Dispatcher -> Runtime : recheck identity and deliver
    end
  end
end

note over Poller,Database
  One poll runs at a time per instance.
  Query failures enter bounded backoff.
  Durable controls remain for later retry.
end note

note over Poller,Runtime
  Post-commit fast paths reuse the same dispatch and deduplication boundary.
  This foundation still requires a local Dispatcher adapter.
end note
@enduml
